    "field": "Climate modeling",
    "problem": "Considerable uncertainties in future agricultural drought projections, stemming from differences among climate models, emission scenarios, and inherent climate variability, challenge the reliable identification of regional drought hotspots and the quantification of future risk.",
    "method": "The authors analyze surface soil moisture outputs from CMIP5 multi-model ensembles under four RCP scenarios to project future agricultural drought characteristics and partition the total projection uncertainty into three sources: internal variability, model uncertainty, and scenario uncertainty.",
    "task": "The task is to project 21st-century agricultural drought, identify hotspots, and quantify associated uncertainties by analyzing surface soil moisture outputs from CMIP5 multi-model ensembles under different climate scenarios.",
